# Optional. Leave this unset and every visitor supplies their own key —
# that is the safest way to run this app publicly.
#
# Set it (locally in .env.local, or as a Vercel environment variable) to power
# the site from a single shared key so visitors can try it without one. When
# set, the API routes are automatically restricted:
#   - rate limited per IP
#   - text sent for embedding/generation must be a genuine excerpt of
#     public/corpus/*.txt, so the endpoints cannot be used as an LLM proxy
# A visitor who supplies their own key bypasses both restrictions.
#
# IMPORTANT: never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would ship the key
# into the browser bundle where anyone could read it.
#
# Set a monthly budget cap at platform.openai.com/settings/organization/limits
# before deploying with a shared key.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
